WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500 align:center
The manuscript is in the centre.
Its saved conversation is on the right.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.000 align:center
Gold marks the revised proof wording.
The conversation stays open beside it.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.500 align:center
One proposal covers more than 50 edits
across eight TeX files.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.500 align:center
The proposed proof points to Appendix A.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.000 align:center
Before and proposed text sit side by side.
The record links to the later revision.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.667 align:center
This staged edit asks when
each round costs the same.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:30.958 align:center
The author makes the condition clear.
Price each split by its area.

00:00:30.958 --> 00:00:38.000 align:center
Accept saves the author’s wording.
Undo is still available.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000 align:center
A separate run splits one square
into 256 cells in four rounds.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.000 align:center
The same 85 splits cost 4 by area
and 15 by wall length, in first-split units.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.750 align:center
The CSV saves each round’s totals.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.500 align:center
The plot links back to the run.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:00.000 align:center
The rebuilt manuscript contains
the computed plot and its caption.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.000 align:center
In this example, an independent review
can send the wording back for revision.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.000 align:center
The arXiv check rebuilds the saved
draft from an 11-file package.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000 align:center
Both LaTeX passes succeed.
All 21 pages reproduce the same text.
